---
// Schematic of the Experiment 2-2 heatmap patterns: a 12×12 lower-triangular grid banded system/tools | user | <think> | answer,
// with callouts for the attention sink, reasoning triangle, output triangle and position bias (redraw of Fig 2-7; not measured values).
---

<svg
	class="dg"
	viewBox="0 0 720 604"
	role="img"
	aria-labelledby="d2-ahs-title d2-ahs-desc"
	style="min-width: 630px"
>
	<title id="d2-ahs-title">Attention heatmap patterns (schematic)</title>
	<desc id="d2-ahs-desc">
		A schematic lower-triangular attention heatmap, not measured values. Rows are Queries and columns are Keys, and
		both axes are divided into four bands in sequence order: system prompt and tools, user message, the model's
		reasoning inside think tags, and the answer. Darker cells mean more attention. Four patterns are called out.
		Attention sink: the first column is dark in every row, because the first token often absorbs an abnormally high
		share of attention weight. Reasoning triangle: the think rows attend to earlier reasoning and to the tool
		definitions. Output triangle: the answer rows form another triangle and attend to the reasoning trace. Position
		bias: recall is higher for information at the beginning and end of the context, and information in the middle is
		more likely to be overlooked.
	</desc>
	<defs>
		<marker id="d2-ahs-arrow" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5" markerWidth="8" markerHeight="8" orient="auto-start-reverse">
